{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"singular value decomposition singular value decomposition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md","fileName":"Singular Value Decomposition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Singular Value Decomposition","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Numerical Eigenvalue Methods]] · [[Distance Geometry and Dimension Reduction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Numerical Eigenvalue Methods","Distance Geometry and Dimension Reduction","Pseudoinverse","Least Squares Approximation","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"singular value decomposition singular value decomposition","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Singular Value Decomposition.md","fileName":"Singular Value Decomposition.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Singular Value Decomposition","heading":"Singular Value Decomposition","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Singular value decomposition factors a real matrix as $A=UDV^T$, where $U$ and $V$ are orthogonal and $D$ is diagonal or rectangular diagonal with nonnegative singular values.\n\nUnlike eigenvalue decomposition, SVD applies to rectangular matrices. It exposes rank and conditioning and provides stable formulas for the [[Pseudoinverse]] and [[Least Squares Approximation]].\n\nFor high-dimensional data, the source orders the transformed directions by decreasing sum of squares. Retaining the leading directions cr